Bound the Keystone session of the quota project lookup

`_keystone_client` (cinder/api/api_utils.py) builds the session the quota
code looks a project and its hierarchy up through, with the token of the
request it serves. It takes the TLS options of `[keystone_authtoken]` and
passes no timeout, so the session has none, and no option of cinder.conf
reaches it. A lookup whose Keystone stops answering on an established
connection then waits out the kernel's retransmission limit
(`tcp_retries2 = 15`, about 15.6 minutes) and holds the API worker that
serves the request. On 2026-11-17 Barbican requests behind a killed
Keystone pod hung for 939 to 952 seconds the same way (#1799).

The patch passes `timeout=CONF.keystone_authtoken.http_connect_timeout`
to the session, the bound the cinder-operator renders as `10` for the
token middleware. keystoneauth applies it as both the connect and the read
timeout; the lookup passes no retries, so it fails after 10 seconds. With
the option unset the session gets `timeout=None`, which is what it gets
today.

Tests: no upstream test pins the arguments of the session; the existing
tests in cinder/tests/unit/test_quota_utils.py mock it and assert the auth
plugin only. The patch adds two tests there that assert the `timeout`
argument with the option set and unset, and both fail without it.

Proof: tests/container-images/verify_cinder.sh asserts in the built image
that `_keystone_client` passes `timeout=7` with
`[keystone_authtoken] http_connect_timeout = 7` and `timeout=None` with the
option unset.

The 2026.2 twin is 0008 of the same name, cut from 29.0.0.

Applies to cinder 28.0.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

diff --git a/cinder/api/api_utils.py b/cinder/api/api_utils.py
index 4a21381..23819bf 100644
--- a/cinder/api/api_utils.py
+++ b/cinder/api/api_utils.py
@@ -205,6 +205,7 @@ def _keystone_client(context: 'context.RequestContext',
         cacert=CONF.keystone_authtoken.cafile,
         key=CONF.keystone_authtoken.keyfile,
         cert=CONF.keystone_authtoken.certfile,
+        timeout=CONF.keystone_authtoken.http_connect_timeout,
         split_loggers=CONF.service_user.split_loggers)
     return client.Client(auth_url=CONF.keystone_authtoken.auth_url,
                          session=client_session, version=version)
diff --git a/cinder/tests/unit/test_quota_utils.py b/cinder/tests/unit/test_quota_utils.py
index 35aae9f..56c6c02 100644
--- a/cinder/tests/unit/test_quota_utils.py
+++ b/cinder/tests/unit/test_quota_utils.py
@@ -48,6 +48,23 @@ class QuotaUtilsTest(test.TestCase):
                                                session=ksclient_session(),
                                                version=(3, 0))
 
+    @mock.patch('keystoneclient.client.Client')
+    @mock.patch('keystoneauth1.session.Session')
+    def test_keystone_client_session_timeout(self, ksclient_session,
+                                             ksclient_class):
+        self.fixture.config(http_connect_timeout=7,
+                            group='keystone_authtoken')
+        api_utils._keystone_client(self.context)
+        self.assertEqual(7, ksclient_session.call_args.kwargs['timeout'])
+
+    @mock.patch('keystoneclient.client.Client')
+    @mock.patch('keystoneauth1.session.Session')
+    def test_keystone_client_session_timeout_unset(self, ksclient_session,
+                                                   ksclient_class):
+        api_utils._keystone_client(self.context)
+        self.assertIn('timeout', ksclient_session.call_args.kwargs)
+        self.assertIsNone(ksclient_session.call_args.kwargs['timeout'])
+
     @mock.patch('keystoneclient.client.Client')
     @mock.patch('keystoneauth1.session.Session')
     @mock.patch('keystoneauth1.identity.Token')
